            "text": "{\"packet_id\":\"B004\",\"decisions\":[{\"criterion\":\"Input/expected-output schema\",\"label\":\"partially-documented\",\"evidence_refs\":[{\"source_id\":\"E001\",\"line_start\":133,\"line_end\":137},{\"source_id\":\"E001\",\"line_start\":196,\"line_end\":199},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":148,\"line_end\":155},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":292,\"line_end\":305},{\"source_id\":\"E003\",\"line_start\":37,\"line_end\":45}],\"evidence_note\":\"README and code show samples as .jsonl with fields like task_id, solution/completion, _identifier and describe output file names, but no complete, formal schema for all fields or evaluation JSON structure is provided.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"criterion\":\"Metric definition\",\"label\":\"claimed-but-not-verifiable\",\"evidence_refs\":[{\"source_id\":\"E001\",\"line_start\":133,\"line_end\":137},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":29,\"line_end\":34},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":214,\"line_end\":223},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":257,\"line_end\":258}],\"evidence_note\":\"The code imports estimate_pass_at_k and references pass@k and gt_pass_rate, but the implementation or formal definition of these metrics is in bigcodebench.eval, which is not included in the packet.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"criterion\":\"Evaluator implementation available\",\"label\":\"partially-documented\",\"evidence_refs\":[{\"source_id\":\"E001\",\"line_start\":112,\"line_end\":137},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":87,\"line_end\":115},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":117,\"line_end\":205},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":242,\"line_end\":266},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":285,\"line_end\":323}],\"evidence_note\":\"Core evaluation logic, including local, gradio, and e2b execution, ground-truth caching, and sample processing is implemented. However, crucial pieces (untrusted_check, estimate_pass_at_k, PASS, compatible_eval_result) live in bigcodebench.eval, which is not present.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"criterion\":\"Grading rules & tie-breaking\",\"label\":\"claimed-but-not-verifiable\",\"evidence_refs\":[{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":29,\"line_end\":34},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":285,\"line_end\":323}],\"evidence_note\":\"Evaluation aggregates per-sample results and uses estimate_pass_at_k and PASS from bigcodebench.eval, but the exact grading rules (e.g., how multiple samples per task, errors, or ties are handled) are encapsulated in missing code.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"criterion\":\"Predictions->aggregate-score mapping\",\"label\":\"claimed-but-not-verifiable\",\"evidence_refs\":[{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":285,\"line_end\":323},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":214,\"line_end\":223},{\"source_id\":\"E002\",\"line_start\":257,\"line_end\":258}],\"evidence_note\":\"We see how individual solutions are checked and collected, but the final computation of pass@k and overall scores is delegated to estimate_pass_at_k in bigcodebench.eval, whose implementation is not shown.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"criterion\":\"Sample predictions / trajectories\",\"label\":\"claimed-but-not-verifiable\",\"evidence_refs\":[{\"source_id\":\"E001\",\"line_start\":187,\"line_end\":191},{\"source_id\":\"E003\",\"line_start\":37,\"line_end\":45}],\"evidence_note\":\"README states pre-generated LLM code samples are available in a release archive, and syncheck.py describes how to load such samples, but the actual sample files are not included in this packet.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}]}"
